<script>
import OpenApiOperation from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/OpenApiOperation.abide'
import openApiOperationSource from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/OpenApiOperation.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import openApiOperationTestSource from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/OpenApiOperation.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import searchContactsSource from 'crm/src/assistant/searchContacts.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="OpenAPI is generated from the handler files">
        <Example
            id="openapi"
            app="crm"
            title="`/__abide/openapi.json` — the operation, from the handler file"
            summary="A partner's integration wants the CRM's contact search as an OpenAPI operation. Read the app's document: the operation carries the handler's sentence and its typed argument."
            files={{
                'src/assistant/lib/OpenApiOperation.abide': openApiOperationSource,
                'src/assistant/searchContacts.handler.ts': searchContactsSource,
                'src/assistant/lib/OpenApiOperation.test.ts': openApiOperationTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <OpenApiOperation />
        </Example>

        <p>Nobody wrote the operation. The parameter is the handler's argument type and the
            description is its <code>description</code> option, so the document cannot describe a
            handler that is not there. A handler added is an operation published, with no step to
            rerun.</p>

        <p>The document is OpenAPI 3.1, whose schema dialect is JSON Schema, so a handler's schema
            is published as it is. The test reads the same document from <code>createApp</code>, in
            process.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>What it does for the CRM</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>OpenApiDocument</code></td><td>The type of the document, for code that reads it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>abide openapi [--url &lt;origin&gt;]</code></td><td>Prints the document from the source, for a spec committed beside the code. <code>--url</code> asks a running deployment instead.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>abide:openapi</code></td><td>The log namespace that warns when a handler's schema has no JSON Schema of its own.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <Code code={`abide openapi > openapi.json`} />
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
